==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* High damage.
* Good for [[PvP]].
* Reasonably good for grinding.
* Most moves have long range.
* All moves are multi-target, except {{Ability|X}} (Tapped) and {{Ability|V}} (Tapped).
* Most moves can damage [[Sea Beast]]s.
* Grants user a powerful second life that gives an opportunity to make a comeback, with good players being able to easily wipe entire servers, staying effectively immortal.
** Provides a huge damage reduction (60%).
** Grants a great speed, [[Dash|dash]] and [[Air Jump|jump]] buff.
** Cooldowns are drastically reduced.

|{{Ability|TAP}}
* Great damage.
* Decent combo potential.
* '''Last Stand:''' Extremely high damage output.

|{{Ability|Z}}
* Great range.
* Very high burst damage.
* Very effective against large enemies as this attack ignores part of defense buffs.
* '''Tapped (upgraded):''' Good for dealing chip damage and cancelling opponent's attacks from afar, mainly due to the additional Pain Ghosts that it spawns.

|{{Ability|X}}
* Great combo follow-up, especially with knockback skills.
* Decent hitbox.
* Decent mobility. 
* High damage, especially on the held variant.
* '''Last Stand:''' Short charge time.

|{{Ability|C}}
* Amazing range.
* Good hitbox.
* Great damage.
* Great combo potential.
* Amazing stun.
* '''Tapped:''' Fast projectile.
* '''Last Stand:''' Very short charge time.

|{{Ability|V}}
* High stun, especially when held.
* Large hitbox, sometimes it lands without even being near the opponent.
* Can be further held to increase the hitbox/AoE and damage.
* Blinds and distorts the vision of the enemy.
* '''Tapped:''' High range and fast projectile speed.
* '''Last Stand:''' Doesn't consume Pain Meter.

|{{Ability|F}}
* Has a short cooldown, which makes it good for PvP and escaping one-shot combos.
* Can be instantly refilled with '''Pain Ghosts''', allowing for quick traversal.
* '''Tapped:''' The teleportation range is slightly longer than other fruits with similar moves.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* High mastery requirements.
** The upgrades are expensive and have even higher mastery requirements.
* All of the moves can leave the user vulnerable if they hold them for too long.
* Requires precise aim at long range.
* All moves are hard to hit in aerial combat.
* Despite giving a second life, the user will only survive if the enemy is killed within 30 seconds. (60 when upgraded)
** Finisher move(like [[Dragon Talon]] Z and [[Shadow]] C) and [[Water]] can bypass this passive.

|{{Ability|TAP}}
* Short range.
* Untrue stun (Enemies can still use abilities whilst being hit).
* Last hit deals absurdly high knockback.

|{{Ability|Z}}
* Small direct hitbox.
* Vulnerable during prolonged usage (Should only be held for 3 seconds maximum).
* Although this move can be held indefinitely, both the speed and damage will gradually worsen after a few seconds of the move being held.

|{{Ability|X}}
* Short dash range.
* Opponents can still use M1 attacks while stunned.
* '''Tapped:''' Single-target.
** Cannot [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]].
* '''Held:''' The beam is not guaranteed to deal damage, although this is rare.

|{{Ability|C}}
* Medium start-up time, giving opponents the opportunity to escape.
* Small direct hitbox.
* The knockback trajectory can make combos more difficult, such as having to aim [[Godhuman]]'s {{Ability|Godhuman|Z}} at the enemy.
* '''Held (upgraded):''' Takes a while to fully charge.
** Requires practice to use in active PvP.

|{{Ability|V}}
* Low tick damage.
* No cooldown reduction.
* '''Tapped:''' Single-target.
* '''Held:''' The projectiles is slow.
** Has a long start-up.
** Drains the Pain Meter.
* '''Last Stand:''' Charges too quickly, and mostly executes as the held version instead.

|{{Ability|F}}
* '''Held (upgraded):''' The second part of the attack can be hard to control effectively.
}}
</tabber>

