==Notes==
* {{Ability|V}} is a good [[Instinct Break]] move due to enemies taking continuous tick damage after being hit by the move. Some [[sword]] and [[gun]] users use it solely for this reason.
* It may be more effective to use than other fruits like [[Ice]] if not a [[fruit]] main, as Ice's combos can easily be [[Instinct]]-tricked (unless they have [[Cyborg]] V3), while {{Ability|V}} makes combos impossible to [[Instinct]]-trick.
* It is recommended to use Pain as a fruit main, as '''Last Stand''', while a useful second life, locks the player into using only the fruit, rendering their other weapons useless, which could be a huge hindrance without any [[stats]] invested into [[Blox Fruit]].
* {{Ability|Z}} should be timed, as after a point it becomes slow and punishable. The user should try and only use it for '''3-4 seconds''' to maximize it's use.
* Due to '''Last Stand''' being considered a transformation, the user is incapable of activating their [[Race Awakening]] after the mode activates.
* Like other transformations, [[Race Awakening]] can still be activated before '''Last Stand''' is activated and it will persist , until it runs out or the player dies.
* Despite '''Last Stand''' giving the user a second life, they should be wary if they are fighting a [[Cyborg]] user, as if they happen to die to their V3 [[Energy Core]] or its awakened electricity passives, it will kill the user without triggering their second life.
* '''Last Stand''' will not activate if the user was killed by the ocean, despite water damage being able to fill the Pain Meter.
* During a [[Raids|Raid]], the user can absorb '''Pain Ghosts''', meaning that the user can build the '''Pain Meter''' by taking damage or absorbing '''Pain Ghosts.'''
* While '''Last Stand''' is active, there is no way to fill the Pain Meter, even if '''Pain Ghosts''' are absorbed or damage is taken.
* There is a trick to avoid losing [[Bounty and Honor System|bounty/honor]] when the user is still in '''Last Stand''' while [[Bounty and Honor System|"In Combat - Bounty/Honor at risk!"]]. If the user lets themselves to be hit by [[Enemies|enemy]] multiple times (3 - 4 hits) right after '''Last Stand''' ends, the death will be counted as [[PvP mechanics|Suspicious Kill]].
* Agony Nuke Held in Last Stand form can be paired with Ghoul's V3 and V4 cooldown reduction to be able to have a 1 second cooldown, making it spammable.
* The Pain Ghost unupgraded also seeks toward enemies but shorter.

==Grinding==
* Although Pain possesses great power and potential, it is not recommended for grinding in [[First Sea]] to the early [[Second Sea]] due to the 4th M1 having very high knockback and very demanding [[mastery]].
* However, if one wishes to grind using the Pain fruit;
** They may repeatedly spam M1 and on the 4th one, dash and M1 again. This has a chance to pick the enemy up again and repeat the cycle again (This tactic may also be used for PvP)
** 3 M1, Long held X, Tapped or Held C, 3 M1 (wait for NPC to come down), Held Z, Tapped V. (If don't have [V] Torturing Pulse, the user can use the 1st part of the combo)
** 4 M1, Tapped X, Dash, 3 M1, Tapped C, Held or Tapped V, Held Z directly at the NPC, F, 4 M1, (Cycle again)
** Use M1 and moves against a wall or high solid object.

==Trivia==
* Along with a few other [[fruits]], Pain (named Paw at the time) was in the [[Raids|Fruit Awakening]] straw poll of {{Update|14}}. 
** However, [[Rumble]] received the most votes, resulting in Pain getting no [[Raids|awakening]], but note that Rumble now is changed to [[Lightning]] and has no awakening. Pain and [[Lightning]] both now have a [[Admin Panel]] Upgrade System.
* Tapped {{Ability|C}} shares the same death skull effect as Acidum Rifle's {{Ability|Acidum Rifle|Z}}, the only difference being in size and color.
* Pain has its own death animation when '''Last Stand''' is activated.
* Pain is the second fruit to have revive/second life mechanic, the first being [[Ghost]] Fruit.
* {{Ability|V}} has the same mesh as [[Sanguine Art]]'s {{Ability|Sanguine Art|C}}.
* The first boss to use the reworked pain fruit is [[Agony]] (not counting the tormented bosses from the pain event).
* The user's ability [[GUI]] gains a red hue when they're in '''Last Stand'''.
* There is a little bit of blood on the edge of Pain Fruit's bandages.
* The Pain Ghosts will prioritize refilling the user if they are within closer proximity, regardless if they were targeting an opponent with '''Torment Conductor''' unlocked.
* The inventory icon is a Pain Ghost.
* The {{CHROMATIC}} skins released in the [[Summer Gacha]] refer to emotions:
** {{Skin|Sadness}}'s colour scheme, which consists primarily of blue, refers to how the colour blue is commonly associated with sadness or feelings of isolation.
** {{Skin|Torment}} is an emotion that involves extreme mental distress and anguish. The dark crimson is similar to Pain's original colour scheme, both being shades of red. This is further tied in with the name of Pain's original colour {{Skin|Agony}}, which is also a synonym for severe emotional or mental suffering. The colour scheme of this chromatic is similar to blood.
** {{Skin|Frustration}}'s colour scheme is similar to fire, referencing how both fire and anger are intense, potentially destructive, and escalate quickly.
* The '''Last Stand''' passive is capable of outspeeding bounty hunt exploiters.
* The Pain fruit is the only fruit in the entire game to have a variant to all of its moves.
* Pain’s default skin, {{Skin|Agony}}, is a reference to the [[Raid Bosses|Raid Boss]], [[Agony]], which also uses the Pain [[Blox Fruits|fruit]], who rivaled [[Ashen]] in the Summer Expansion 2025 Trailer ([[Updates/27.0|Update 27]]).
* Pain used to be considered one of the worst {{Legendary|Legendary}} fruits, but now due to its rework it is high valued and generally considered a good fruit for grinding.

